  - T-cell receptor
  - B-cell receptor
  - repertoire sequencing
  - single-cell RNA-seq
  - somatic hypermutation
  - clonal expansion
  - reproducible research
  - R
abstract: >-
  A set of configuration-driven R workflows for adaptive immune receptor
  repertoire (AIRR) analysis and the single-cell transcriptome analyses that
  accompany it. Four pipelines cover single-cell TCR repertoires, single-cell
  BCR repertoires including clonal inference and somatic hypermutation, bulk
  TCR/BCR repertoires with differential clonal abundance testing, and
  single-cell gene expression. The workflows are written to be applied to any
  cohort: study-specific labels, thresholds and contrasts are supplied through
  a single configuration file, and the analytical decisions that are easy to
  get wrong in repertoire work (abundance floors, rarefaction to common
  sequencing depth, separation of descriptive category from statistical
  significance, attainable power at small sample size) are made explicit and
  diagnosable.
